Micropolis Ubuntu source package notes
======================================

Frozen upstream web deployment
------------------------------

The Debian package build deliberately does not invoke Node.js, pnpm, Vite or
Emscripten. Instead, debian/vendor/micropolis-web contains the exact static
application files selected from upstream's published gh-pages deployment.
The deployment commit records that it was generated from source commit
c591573ad8c8c8bbecf26cea018e2c164c22c252; full provenance is recorded in
debian/vendor/BUILDINFO.

This design is required for the Ubuntu 24.04 Noble package to build offline on
all target architectures. In particular, Noble does not publish its nodejs
binary package for i386, while the newer Micropolis frontend toolchain also
requires a newer Node.js than Noble provides. Making package builds consume a
frozen upstream-published deployment avoids network access and avoids an
architecture-dependent JavaScript build dependency.

Architecture: any is intentional
--------------------------------

Although the installed HTML, JavaScript, data and WebAssembly payload is not
host-architecture-specific, the micropolis-core binary package is deliberately
Architecture: any. The purpose is to make Launchpad schedule and test this
source package independently on every enabled target architecture, including
i386 and s390x, rather than building one Architecture: all package only once.

Updating the package
--------------------

When moving to another upstream snapshot:

  1. identify a published static deployment and the exact source commit that
     generated it;
  2. replace debian/vendor/micropolis-web with that matching deployment;
  3. update debian/vendor/BUILDINFO and debian/changelog together;
  4. verify that the deployment still uses the /MicropolisCore base path;
  5. run the package smoke test and a clean sbuild for every supported target.

Do not replace the frozen deployment with a networked npm/pnpm build in
debian/rules: Launchpad package builds are expected to be self-contained.
